      "id": "kn1r3a8",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Constitutional Articles Related to the Supreme Court"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Article 131 specifies the Original Jurisdiction of the Supreme Court regarding federal disputes.",
        "Article 143 details the Advisory Jurisdiction, enabling the President of India to consult the Supreme Court.",
        "The constitutional provisions define the appointment, qualifications, tenure, and removal procedures for Supreme Court judges.",
        "The Supreme Court exercises comprehensive authority across Original, Appellate, Advisory, and Writ Jurisdictions."
      ],
      "id": "kie5sek"
    },
